{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And they shall bear them the iniquity of guilt.</b> They themselves, when they consecrated the hallowed thing, made it so that they would be guilty if they commit sacrilege therein by deriving benefit from it — and the rule that 'the mouth that forbade is the mouth that permitted' does not apply. The reason for this is <i>for I am YHWH who sanctifies them</i> (Leviticus 22:32): since they consecrated the thing, I, YHWH, sanctify it, and no human hand can nullify its sanctity."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:15.717868636Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}